#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119516 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74764043-e1e7-56d6-8f53-9d287a30e538" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant After Switching Two Rows"}] :question/id #uuid "596aa514-d598-5ffe-affe-f5580d130bd0" :question/math-academy-id "e-4422" :question/problem "Suppose $A$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix and $\\det (A) = -16$. The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operation $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2$ (switching the first and the second rows). What is the value of $\\det(B)$?" :question/worked-solution "Since swapping any two rows changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite sign, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(B) &= -det(A) \\\\\n&= - (-16) \\\\\n&= 16\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119517 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f11b223-edd2-59b8-b761-164d56e29746" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant After Multiplying a Row by a Number"}] :question/id #uuid "89152146-8f04-5b4f-8436-15b82431c35d" :question/math-academy-id "e-4423" :question/problem "Suppose $A$ is a $6 \\times 6$ matrix and $\\det(A) = 32$. The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operation $R_3:= \\dfrac{1}{8} R_3$. What is the value of $\\det(B)$?" :question/worked-solution "The row operation applied to $A$ consists of multiplying a row by the number\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{8}\n$$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(B) &= \\frac{1}{8}det(A) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{8} \\cdot 32 \\\\\n&= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119518 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "24e5e193-5e30-5480-9e5d-b7b8f1d5de87" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant After Applying Several Elementary Operations"}] :question/id #uuid "6d46c442-4675-5e0e-a834-a8b10ad2b86a" :question/math-academy-id "e-4424" :question/problem "Suppose $A$ is an $8 \\times 8$ matrix and $\\det(A) = 5$. The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operations $R_4 \\leftrightarrow R_5$, $R_6:= 4 R_6$, and $R_8: = R_8 - \\dfrac{1}{2} R_7$. What is the value of $\\det(B)$?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation $R_4 \\leftrightarrow R_5$ involves swapping two rows, so it changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\n- The operation $R_6:= 4 R_6$ involves multiplying a row by $4$, so the determinant is multiplied by $4$ as well.\n- The operation $R_8:= R_8 - \\dfrac{1}{2} R_7$ involves adding a multiple of one row to another row, so it does not change the determinant.\n\nTherefore, we have to change the sign of the determinant to the opposite one and multiply by $4$ as well. Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(B) &= 4 \\cdot (-det(A)) \\\\\n&=-4det(A) \\\\\n&=-4 \\cdot 5 \\\\\n&=-20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119589 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a0ab53e-79ff-5520-bb50-069fd381d29d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Row Operation Given the Connection Between Two Determinants"}] :question/id #uuid "cbd9b4bc-146a-57f7-a03f-f045f86f3c21" :question/math-academy-id "e-6143" :question/problem "Given that $\\det(X)=\\det(Y)$, which elementary row operations transforms matrix $X$ to matrix $Y$, where\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "Since\n\n$$\n\\det(X)=\\det(Y)\n$$\n\n, the row operation applied to $X$ must be to add or subtract a multiple of one row to another row. In other words, it is of the form\n\n$$\nR_j:= R_j + (k)R_i, \\quad i \\neq j\n$$\n\nBy considering the given row operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(X) &= \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\mid R_{2}\\begin{vmatrix}:=R_{2} + 3R_{3} \\\\ =\\end{vmatrix}2\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}2 \\\\\n&= - 1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= det(Y)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\nR_2:= R_2 + 3R_3\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119590 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "272d9a54-ba97-5175-86df-0a78337da7b9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant After Multiplying a Matrix by a Scalar"}] :question/id #uuid "ce910ef2-c3af-5173-84d4-ee2a4c957954" :question/math-academy-id "e-6148" :question/problem "Suppose $A$ is a $4\\times4$ matrix and $\\det(A)=5$. What is the value of $\\det(2A)$?" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k$, and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\ndet(k \\cdot A) = k^{n} \\cdot det(A)\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=2$ and $n=4$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(2A) &= 2^{4} \\cdot det(A) \\\\\n&= 16 \\cdot 5 \\\\\n&= 80\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120347 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a0ab53e-79ff-5520-bb50-069fd381d29d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Row Operation Given the Connection Between Two Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "890be7e4-f4c9-5c96-bdb5-907d133c3a2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R_{3}↔R_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118558} {:answer/id #uuid "bb30654d-6dbd-5a98-9d7b-f56d8c76ab08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R_{2}:=R_{2} + (-1)R_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118559} {:answer/id #uuid "be284e31-2dec-58ef-a1b4-ba706b77a7e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R_{3}:=R_{3} + 2R_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118560} {:answer/id #uuid "09554b64-dd0c-576e-8398-8157325d10c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R_{2}:=R_{2} + (-2)R_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118561} {:answer/id #uuid "54b8f081-9585-57a6-817e-520d97437321" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R_{3}:=\\frac{1}{2}R_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118562}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09554b64-dd0c-576e-8398-8157325d10c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R_{2}:=R_{2} + (-2)R_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118561} :answer-field/id #uuid "31331c92-5912-5c03-8535-61333df19ca6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118557}] :question/id #uuid "1d4250d6-4c9c-5a2c-ac92-71ea5c8419b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-42076" :question/problem "Given that $det(A) = det(B)$, which of the following elementary row operations transforms matrix $A$ to matrix $B$, where\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120359 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "24e5e193-5e30-5480-9e5d-b7b8f1d5de87" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant After Applying Several Elementary Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94d0a1cf-04e3-5846-9d7c-1d524a76e697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118630} {:answer/id #uuid "9f59af76-89cd-5337-98b9-11c25feb57bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118631} {:answer/id #uuid "a5c35b4a-d7e4-5562-96bc-47ad22b45940" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118632} {:answer/id #uuid "c0e964ce-8c4e-55f5-a76d-5ec41493c38b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118633} {:answer/id #uuid "0fdf03b9-553c-56b9-8bc3-4aa41d2a792c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118634}] :answer-f